.TH DIPIMETRICS 1 "2026-08-27" "dvbipitools" "dvbipitools Manual"
.SH NAME
dipimetrics \- collect and serve dvbipitools metrics as Prometheus/OpenMetrics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dipimetrics
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dipimetrics
is a host-level metrics collector for
.BR dipitvhead (1),
.BR dipiradiohead (1),
.BR dipisds (1),
.BR dipibcg (1),
.BR dipirist (1),
.BR dipirec (1),
.BR dipidescramble (1),
.BR dipicam378 (1),
.BR dipifccret (1),
.BR dipisrt (1)
and
.BR dipixy (1).
Each of these, if started with its own
.B \-\-metrics-id
option, periodically sends a snapshot of its own counters.
A snapshot replaces the previous one only once it has arrived completely.
Upgrade
.B dipimetrics
before the exporters: an older
.B dipimetrics
rejects snapshots from newer exporters.
.B dipimetrics
retains the latest snapshot per (component, instance) pair and serves
them all as one Prometheus/OpenMetrics text document at
.B GET /metrics
over plain HTTP.
.PP
A snapshot with a sequence number not greater than the last one seen for
the same (component, instance) is dropped as stale/out of order. A
different process start time is treated as the exporter having
restarted, and is always accepted, replacing all prior state for that
instance. Malformed, oversized, or unsupported-protocol-version
datagrams are rejected outright. Up to 64 instances are tracked
concurrently; a 65th distinct (component, instance) pair is dropped and
logged under
.BR \-v .
An instance that has not sent a snapshot in
.BR \-e / \-\-expiry
seconds is dropped entirely, rather than serving an arbitrarily stale
last-known value.
.PP
The receiving socket is
.BR SOCK_DGRAM ,
bound and never blocked on: a slow or absent collector never affects
the exporters, which are already best-effort senders themselves.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-sock\ \fI<path>\fR
Unix datagram socket to receive snapshots on. Default:
.IR /run/dvbipitools/metrics.sock .
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-listen\ \fI<addr>\fR:\fI<port>\fR
HTTP listen address:port. Default:
.BR 127.0.0.1:9109
(loopback only; use e.g.
.B \-l\ 0.0.0.0:9109
to listen on all interfaces).
.TP
.B \-\-tls\-cert \fI<path>\fR
Certificate file (PEM). HTTPS on
.B \-l
instead of HTTP. Requires
.B \-\-tls\-key
too. Reloaded on
.BR SIGUSR1 .
.TP
.B \-\-tls\-key \fI<path>\fR
Private key file (PEM). Requires
.B \-\-tls\-cert
too.
.TP
.BI \-\-auth " user\fR:\fBpass"
HTTP Basic Auth for
.B GET /metrics.
Default: off.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-expiry\ \fI<s>\fR
Drop an instance after this many seconds without a new snapshot.
Default:
.BR 30 ,
i.e. 6 missed sends at an exporter's own default 5s
.BR \-\-metrics\-interval .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Log every rejected/dropped snapshot (malformed, unsupported protocol
version, stale sequence, store full) and every HTTP 404, to stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-color \fI<when>\fR
.IR auto | always | never .
Default:
.BR auto .
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemonize
Fork to background after startup, detach from terminal.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config\ \fI<path>\fR
YAML configuration file. Keys mirror the options above. Without this option,
.I /etc/dvbipitools/dipimetrics.yaml
is read if it exists.
.TP
.B \-\-config\-strict
Treat configuration file issues (unknown or duplicate keys, invalid values,
conflicting settings, unreadable referenced files) as errors instead of
warnings.
.TP
.B \-\-configtest
Check the configuration file (from
.B \-c
or the default location) and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.SH HTTP ENDPOINT
.BR \-l / \-\-listen
is the address:port
.B GET /metrics
is served on. Every other path returns
.BR 404 .
The server is intentionally minimal: up to 8 connections in flight at
once, a 5-second read/write budget per connection so a stalled client
can't wedge the collector, and
.B Connection: close
on every response. This is a local diagnostics endpoint meant for
infrequent scraping, not a general-purpose web server. Authentication is
off unless
.B \-\-auth
is given, in which case a request missing or mismatching the
.B Authorization
header gets
.BR 401 .
.PP
.BR \-\-tls\-cert / \-\-tls\-key
(PEM, both required together) switch
.B \-l
from plain HTTP to HTTPS. The certificate is reloaded from the same
paths on
.BR SIGUSR1 ,
without dropping the listener or any in-flight connection.
.PP
Output is
.BR application/openmetrics-text :
one
.B # TYPE
/
.B # HELP
pair per metric family actually present (families with zero live
samples are omitted). Every sample carries
.B component="tvhead|radiohead|sds|bcg|rist|rec|descramble|cam378|fccret|srt|xy"
and
.BR headend_id="<the\ exporter's\ \-\-metrics\-id>" ,
plus whatever label the metric itself carries
.RB ( reason ", " input ", " table ", " cas ", " codec ", " transport ", "
.BR peer ", " output ", " mode ", " direction ", " stream ).
The label is deliberately not called
.BR instance :
Prometheus assigns its own
.B instance
label per scrape target (the host:port of
.B dipimetrics
itself), which would collide with and rename an exporter-supplied
.B instance
label to
.BR exported_instance .
.PP
One extra, collector-computed series is added per tracked instance:
.BR dvbipi_metrics_snapshot_age_seconds ,
seconds since that instance's last accepted snapshot, independent of
anything the exporter itself reports.
.PP
.B dipimetrics
also reports on itself, always present regardless of what's currently
tracked:
.BR dvbipi_metrics_instances
(gauge, exporter instances currently held in the store),
.BR dvbipi_metrics_snapshots_received_total
(counter),
.BR dvbipi_metrics_snapshots_rejected_total{reason="malformed|stale|full|version|toolarge"}
(counter, one series per reason),
.BR dvbipi_metrics_snapshots_incomplete_total
(counter, snapshots discarded because a piece of them was lost),
.BR dvbipi_metrics_parts_orphaned_total
(counter, stray snapshot pieces dropped) and
.BR dvbipi_metrics_http_requests_total{status="200|404"}
(counter, one series per status). Each exporter additionally reports
.BR dvbipi_metrics_parts_dropped_total
(counter, snapshot pieces it failed to send).
.SH TRANSPORT STREAM HEALTH
Tools started with
.B \-\-metrics\-inspect\-ts
.I level
(yaml
.BR metrics.inspect-ts ,
needs
.BR \-\-metrics\-id )
report
.B dvbipi_ts_*
series per stream, labeled
.B direction
.RB ( input
or
.BR output )
and
.B stream
.RB ( input0 ", " output0 ", ...)."
The default
.B off
runs and exports nothing.
.TP
.B basic
Sync loss and sync byte errors, transport error packets, continuity errors, PAT, PMT, CAT,
SDT, NIT, EIT present/following, RST and TDT/TOT presence and repetition, PMT-referenced pids
missing, PCR repetition and discontinuities, PTS gaps, packet, null and scrambled counters, stalls,
table versions and last-seen timestamps.
.TP
.B medium
Adds CRC checks of EIT, TOT and BAT, and PCR arrival jitter from kernel receive timestamps on
UDP/RTP inputs.
.TP
.B full
Adds packets and pids the PMT does not reference, and per pid and per service packet and scrambled packet counters
for the pids the PMT references when
.BR \-\-metrics\-inspect\-ts\-pids
is set.
.PP
Counters count since process start. A missing or late table counts once per episode. Series named
.B *_timestamp_seconds
are unix times. The checks follow ETSI TR 101 290 where a receiver can measure them, this is not a
conformance test.
.B dipifccret
and
.B dipixy
report one aggregate
.B input0
with the header-level checks only,
.B dipirist
and
.B dipisrt
the input stream, and
.B dipisrt
as receiver the output too.
.B dipiradiohead
reports its generated output, and an input for every HLS input, whose segments are transport streams.
.B dipirec
reports its input with
.B \-f raw
and
.BR "\-f ts" ,
and with
.B \-f ts
its filtered output too.
A continuity error can also come from packets lost on the receiving host
itself (UDP socket or NIC buffers). The old unlabeled
.B dipitvhead
series with these names are replaced by the labeled ones when the option is on.
.SH SIGNALS
.BR \(haC ,
SIGINT or SIGTERM stop the process: sockets are closed and the Unix
socket file is removed.
.PP
.B SIGUSR1
reloads the TLS certificate/key from the
.BR \-\-tls\-cert / \-\-tls\-key
paths (no-op if HTTPS isn't enabled).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B dipimetrics
Start the collector with defaults.
.TP
.B dipimetrics \-l 0.0.0.0:9109 \-e 60
Reachable from another host, with a longer expiry.
.TP
.B dipimetrics \-l 0.0.0.0:9109 \-\-tls\-cert srv.crt \-\-tls\-key srv.key
Serve over HTTPS.
.TP
.B dipimetrics \-l 0.0.0.0:9109 \-\-auth scraper:hunter2
Require HTTP Basic Auth for the scrape.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success.
A non-zero status is returned on argument errors, configuration file errors
or socket/bind failure.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/dvbipitools/dipimetrics.yaml
Default configuration file, read if present. A commented template with all
defaults ships as
.IR /usr/share/dvbipitools/etc/dipimetrics.yaml .
.TP
.I /run/dvbipitools/metrics.sock
Default Unix datagram socket for receiving snapshots from exporters,
unless overridden with
.BR \-S / \-\-sock .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dipitvhead (1),
.BR dipiradiohead (1),
.BR dipisds (1),
.BR dipibcg (1),
.BR dipirist (1),
